  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Tap **Rec** on the Looper and play. Recording starts on the next downbeat and closes itself after four **Bars**; tap Rec again to overdub over it, and again to just listen. **Undo** takes back the last layer, and a second Undo brings it back.",
      "position": [
        710.0,
        514.0
      ],
      "width": 270.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Your sound reaches the patch a round trip late, the **In** figure in the status bar. **Auto latency** writes each overdub that much earlier, so the layers sit where you played them, not where they arrived.",
      "position": [
        710.0,
        654.0
      ],
      "width": 270.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The click: a rim on every beat and a cowbell on each bar. Mute Mixer channels 1 and 2 once the loop is going. Right-click a footswitch to learn a MIDI pedal.",
      "position": [
        710.0,
        799.0
      ],
      "width": 270.0
    }
  ]
